window.docContents[200].resolve({"/Hoare2/#Hoare-Logic--Hoare2___-Hoare-Logic___-Part-II--Finding-Loop-Invariants--Exercise___-Power-Series":{"contents":"\n\nThis is again a program schema rather than a program.  Why not...\n[[\n      {{ True }}\n    X := 0;\n    Y := 1;\n    Z := 1;\n    while X <> W do\n      Z := 2 * Z;\n      Y := Y + Z;\n      X := X + 1\n    end\n      {{ Y = 2 ^ (W + 1) - 1 }}\n]]\n   ...?\n\n   BCP 21: Ditto my response above.  IMO this is not a problem.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis exercise should really be expanded into its\nown whole section.  Moreover, there is a proposal to make the\ndecorations in Hoare look more like the decorations earlier in the\npresent chapter.  All three should be aligned.\n\n\n\n","context":"Hoare Logic\u0009Hoare2: Hoare Logic, Part II\u0009Finding Loop Invariants","header":"6.3.9. Exercise: Power Series","id":"/Hoare2/#Hoare-Logic--Hoare2___-Hoare-Logic___-Part-II--Finding-Loop-Invariants--Exercise___-Power-Series"}});